{"first_web": "firecrawl", "used_firecrawl": true, "used_native": false, "skills": ["firecrawl", "firecrawl-scrape"], "fc_cmds": ["scrape"], "fc_api": [], "n_tools": 4, "tools": ["shell", "shell", "shell", "shell"], "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 79929, "cached_input_tokens": 58240, "output_tokens": 452}, "cost_usd": 0.0389, "result_subtype": "success", "error": null, "answer": "Anthropic\u2019s [Building effective agents](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents) describes five workflow patterns:\n\n1. **Prompt chaining** \u2014 Split a task into sequential steps, with each LLM call using the previous step\u2019s output. Optional checks validate intermediate results.\n2. **Routing** \u2014 Classify an input and direct it to a specialized prompt, model, or process.\n3. **Parallelization** \u2014 Run LLM calls simultaneously and combine their results. Two variants are **sectioning** (independent subtasks) and **voting** (multiple attempts at the same task).\n4. **Orchestrator-workers** \u2014 A central LLM dynamically determines subtasks, delegates them to worker LLMs, and synthesizes their results.\n5. **Evaluator-optimizer** \u2014 One LLM generates an answer while another evaluates it, providing feedback for iterative improvement.\n\nThe article separately discusses the **augmented LLM** as a foundational building block and **autonomous agents** as systems that dynamically control their own steps and tool use.", "correct": true, "id": "t05", "trial": 1, "duration_s": 16.6, "timed_out": false, "stderr": "Reading additional input from stdin...\n", "outputs": ["README.md", "notes.txt"]}
